  "reason": "Author retired the attribution diagram and its one introductory reference, preserving the provenance example. Coverage paragraph, heading, and caption superseded by the author-approved dynamic-boundary account.",
  "retired_sentence": "\\autoref{attribution-model} shows the information retained for each operation.",
  "retired_tex": "\\begin{figure}[htbp]\n\\centering\n\\includegraphics[width=\\linewidth]{book/latex/assets/attribution-model-7a93d46093.pdf}\n\\caption{\\emph{Attribution provenance model.} Recording the responsible pass and evidence for each edit makes the work traceable after execution. Audit and explanation can use the same history.}\n\\label{attribution-model}\n\\end{figure}\n",
  "superseded_paragraph": "Mechanical checks can determine whether an anchor resolves, an observed dependency belongs to the permitted set, or a generated artifact is current. Semantic claims may still require judgment, and properties left out of the model receive no model-based coverage. When a failure recurs, engineers can ask whether to refine the representation or add a control (\\autoref{model-sync-two-layer-net}).",
  "superseded_caption": "\\emph{Coverage of model correspondence.} Mechanical checks cover only claims the representation makes decidable; semantic claims still require judgment, and unmodeled properties have no model-based coverage.",
